0..75 Comment "// The strings subject\'s shared declarations, imported by every source that"
76..153 Comment "// reads them (`import \"./string-base.gandr\";`): where a string\'s bytes live,"
154..233 Comment "// and the byte lists every claim reads and builds. A string is a value: a copy"
234..310 Comment "// is a new string, and no write to one is seen through another (Racordon et"
311..387 Comment "// al., \"Implementation strategies for mutable value semantics\", _Journal of"
388..459 Comment "// Object Technology_ 21(2), 2022, doi:10.5381/jot.2022.21.2.a2). Short"
460..538 Comment "// strings keep their bytes inline and long ones share a buffer until a write,"
539..594 Comment "// as the C++ and Rust small-string representations do."
596..631 Comment "// The lists the bytes are held in."
632..638 Keyword "import"
639..640 StringLit "\""
